# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# secrets / local env
#
# Runtime credentials live in the process environment, in AWS Secrets Manager,
# or in a local .env that never leaves the machine. `.env.example` is the only
# env file that may be committed, and it holds placeholders only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials
credentials.json
.aws/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# node (console frontend, tui/ TypeScript TUI)
node_modules/
tui/node_modules/
tui/dist/
console/frontend/node_modules/
console/frontend/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
# The built SPA is copied here by the Dockerfile's frontend stage, and by
# `make console-build` on a dev checkout — an emitted artifact, not source.
src/cairn/console/static/

# rust (tui-rs workspace; tui-rs/.gitignore covers it too, kept here so a
# `cargo build` run from the repo root is also covered)
tui-rs/target/

# terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
tfplan
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# tfplan is a saved `terraform plan -out=` file — it can embed the actual
# value of variables marked sensitive=true (the CLI redacts them from
# terminal output, not from the plan file's own contents), so this is a
# secrets-adjacent artifact, not just build noise.
#
# .terraform.lock.hcl is NOT ignored — HashiCorp's own guidance is to
# commit it, so `terraform init` picks the same provider build everywhere.

# lambda build artifacts — scripts/build_reaper_lambda.sh produces these;
# terraform apply reads reaper.zip but neither is source, both are rebuilt
# from lambda/reaper/handler.py + pinned psycopg version on demand.
lambda/*/reaper.zip
lambda/*/.build/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cairn runtime state
#
# `.cairn/` is the per-workspace scratch tree the CLI writes into: the default
# `--output-file` target (`.cairn/out/...`), scout's redacted traces, and the
# gate/eligibility run logs the scripts/ harnesses emit. All of it is
# regenerated by re-running the command that produced it. Committed
# configuration lives in `cairn.yaml` at the repo root, not in here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.cairn/

# os / editor / agent-harness scratch
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/*.lock

# local data / artifacts — never commit vendored datasets or model weights
data/raw/
*.parquet
*.pt
